  "why": "The statement asks for explicit necessary and sufficient conditions. Schmeidler (1956) and Hwang (1981) give general criteria, but on the record's evidence these are implicit: a monodromy/operator condition, or one reached by Picard successive approximation, which Giusteri and Fried say can be written explicitly only in very special cases. The 2024 list still calls the problem open. I read these as reformulations rather than answers to the explicit question, so I scored them none, not whole. Grinevich–Schmidt characterise closure spectrally for one class of curves, so I scored it case. Weiner gives only partial necessary conditions, and I scored it none. The perturbative, approximate, Minkowski, constant-curvature, unboundedness, density, total-curvature and constant-torsion papers ask different questions, so I scored them variant. Bamba–Ogata falls after the snapshot whether it dates from 2025 or 2026. From what the record could read, it builds examples of closed curves from periodic data and states no criterion, so I scored it none. Journal papers count as digested; arXiv preprints whose publication the record does not show count as unreviewed. No event involves AI.",
